<title>INDIA: Indian silver ends sharply lower, gold subdued.</title>
<headline>Indian silver ends sharply lower, gold subdued.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silver prices fell further by close on Friday after opening lower on poor demand, combined with a downtrend in world markets, dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;Improved arrivals of imported silver also pulled prices down,&quot; said a dealer. Silver fell 45 rupees per kg on Thursday.</p>
<p>Gold opened lower, influenced by silver's fall but held steady at that level in limited trade during the day.</p>
<p>Gold biscuits (116.50 grammes each) was steady at 60,300 rupees, retaining the previous day's gain of 50 rupees.</p>
<p>The market will remain closed on Monday for a Hindu festival.</p>
<p>It will reopen on Tuesday.</p>
